<title>USA: U.S. meat output 1.6 pct above a week ago - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. meat output 1.6 pct above a week ago - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Red meat production for week ending Saturday, May 10, rose 1.6 at 818.6 million lbs.-USDA</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING/1  BEEF   CALF/VEAL   PORK/2 LAMB/MUTTON TOTALS/3</p>
<p>10-May-97	507.6     6.5	300.0	4.5	818.6</p>
<p>03-May-97	485.5     6.6	309.1	4.4	805.6</p>
<p>Change:	    4.6%   -1.5%	-2.9%     2.3%	1.6%</p>
<p>11-May-96	516.0     6.4	313.8	4.7	840.9</p>
<p>Change:	   -1.6%    1.6%	-4.4%     4.3%     -2.7%</p>
<p>1997 YTD:     8784.2   118.9     5964.8     92.7    14960.6</p>
<p>1996 YTD:     9111.8   125.8     6291.2    104.7    15633.5</p>
<p>Change:	   -3.6%   -5.5%	-5.2%   -11.5%     -4.3%</p>
<p>LIVESTOCK SLAUGHTER (HEAD)</p>
<p>WEEK ENDING   CATTLE    CALVES/VEALERS    HOGS     SHEEP/LAMBS</p>
<p>10-May-97     737,000	 31,000	 1,599,000	67,000</p>
<p>03-May-97     703,000	 31,000	 1,649,000	66,000</p>
<p>Change:	   4.8%	    0.0%	   -3.0%	  1.5%</p>
<p>11-May-96     739,000	 30,000	 1,691,000	71,000</p>
<p>Change:	  -0.3%	    3.3%	   -5.4%	 -5.6%</p>
<p>1997 YTD:  12,736,000	564,000	31,763,000   1,405,000</p>
<p>1996 YTD:* 12,963,000	594,000	33,894,000   1,595,000</p>
<p>Change:	  -1.8%	   -5.1%	   -6.3%	-11.9%</p>
